<title>FRANCE: Canal Plus details new shareholders.</title>
<headline>Canal Plus details new shareholders.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>French pay TV channel Canal Plus on Tuesday detailed the holdings of its shareholders after the transfer of Compagnie Generale des Eaux's Canal Plus stake to Havas and after the merger of Canal Plus with the European interests of South Africa's Network Holdings Ltd (Nethold).</p>
<p>Nethold is owned by MIH Holdings, Richemont SA and MCL-Multichoice Ltd.</p>
<p>    Shareholder			     Percentage held</p>
<p>    Havas					34.4</p>
<p>    Richemont/MIH			    20.0</p>
<p>    Groupe CDC				  5.4</p>
<p>    Societe Generale			  3.6</p>
<p>    Pathe					 1.3</p>
<p>    Public				     35.3</p>
<p>Note: Canal Plus gave the figures in its newsletter.</p>
</text>
